  "findings": "Inspected Go Botany photographs of pinnate leaves and cane structure, excluding the fruit photograph from the spring model. Added seven-leaflet foliage and arching canes with thinner young twigs, then inspected current small/medium/large pilots and all 36 variants. Open vase and spreading cane outlines span 1.27-2.70 m. This source represents spring leaf flush before the main rose flowering period; there are no autumn hips. Hooked prickles and fine serration remain below 25 mm detail. Accepted as stylized spring dog rose, pending user endorsement.",
